WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.233
Okay!

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:11.433
Which one does NOT belong?

00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:12.067
A.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:12.733
Monday,

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:13.367
B.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:14.000
Tuesday,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.633
C.

00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:15.267
March,

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.567
or D.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:17.200
Friday?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.467
Five seconds!

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:25.467
TIME'S UP!

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.300
The answer is...

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:27.700
C,

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.100
march!

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:28.500
Monday,

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:28.900
Tuesday,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.233
and Friday are all days of

00:00:31.233 --> 00:00:32.033
the week.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.600
March is a month,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.567
so it does not belong.

00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:37.800
Here's one,

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.433
a picture puzzle!

00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:42.133
Which shape completes the pattern?

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:42.667
A.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.300
A filled square,

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:44.833
B.

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:46.467
An empty square,

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.000
C.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.633
A filled triangle,

00:00:48.633 --> 00:00:49.700
or D.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.333
A filled circle?

00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.400
Five seconds!

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.400
TIME'S UP!

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:01.200
The answer is...

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:01.600
A,

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.733
a filled square!

00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:05.000
The rule is the shape gets

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.300
filled in but stays the same

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:07.667
shape,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.933
so the empty square becomes a

00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:10.700
filled square.

00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:13.067
Here's one,

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.867
a number series!

00:01:14.867 --> 00:01:15.467
One,

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:16.067
four,

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:16.667
five,

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:17.267
nine,

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:17.867
fourteen,

00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:19.067
and then...

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.867
what comes next?

00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:21.467
A.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.067
Nineteen,

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:22.667
B.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:23.267
Twenty-eight,

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:23.867
C.

00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:24.467
Twenty-three,

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.667
or D.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:26.267
Twenty?

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:27.467
Five seconds!

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.467
TIME'S UP!

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.467
The answer is...

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:36.900
C,

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:37.333
twenty-three!

00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:39.967
Add the two numbers before it:

00:01:39.967 --> 00:01:42.167
nine plus fourteen is twenty-three.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.800
Each number is the sum of

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.567
the two before it.

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:48.133
So,

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:50.167
are you smart or fart?

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.600
Count up your correct answers to

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.800
find your rank!

00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:55.300
So,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.700
how did you do?

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.067
Comment your score below,

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.433
and follow for more!
